# Shell scripts must always use LF line endings, regardless of the
# committer's platform or core.autocrlf setting. A CRLF shebang/line-ending
# in a shell script breaks `exec bash script.sh` in Linux containers
# (`unable to exec bash\r`, exit 127) — this caused the v0.8.1 Docker boot
# crash (issue #34): the container reported state=started/cpu=0 with empty
# logs because bash itself never started. Same fix pattern as
# garets-config#934.
*.sh text eol=lf
